REAL ESTATE PURCHASE AGREEMENT
This Real Estate Purchase Agreement is made this
dayof
_,2013, between W. E. Dinneen, Inc., a corporation organized under the
laws of the State of Wyoming, having its principal office at 400West 16th Street, Cheyenne,
Wyoming 82001 ("Seller"), and the City of Cheyenne, a municipal corporation organized under
the laws of the State of Wyoming, having its principal officeat 2101ONeilvenue, Cheyenne,
Wyoming 82001 ("Purchaser").The Seller and Purchaser are individually referred to as a
"Party”and collectively referred to as“Parties."
RECITALS
A.Seller is the owner of fee simple title to various parcels of real property generally
located within Block 353, Original City, between Pioneer and Thomes Avenues and between17h
and 18th Streets, Cheyenne, Wyoming, legally described in Exhibit A, which is attached to and
made a part of this Agreement by this reference.Said parcels of real property are hereinafter
generally referred to asthe“Land."
B. One of the parcels of real property described in Exhibit A (Parcel No. 1) is
improved by a building (the“Building"）and other improvements (collectively, with the
Building, the “Improvements") including, but not limited to, all mechanical, plumbing, heating,
ventilating, air-conditioning, electrical fixtures, equipment, and systems located in or on the
constructed upon the other parcels of real property described in Exhibit A (Parcels 2, 3, and 4).
C.With respect to the Land and the Improvements, Seller also owns certain service
and maintenance contracts, equipment leases, and other contracts (collectively, the “Contracts");
certain permits, licenses, certificates of occupancy, and other rights granted by governmental
agencies and entities (collectively,“Permits"); and certain warranties and guaranties
(collectively, the“Warranties"). The Land, the Improvements, the Contracts, the Permits and the
Warranties are hereinafter collectively referred to as the“"Property."
D.Purchaser wishes to purchase the Property from Seller, and Seller is willing to sell
the Property to Purchaser, subject to certain terms and conditions.
E.Seller and Purchaser wish to set forth in writing the terms of their agreement
relating to the foregoing.
In consideration of the matters described above, and of the mutual benefits and
obligations setforth in this Agreement, the Parties agree asfollows:
```

